 sentence and the docblock terminator line.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"C10\\\",\\n      \\\"source_id\\\": \\\"deepseek_readme\\\",\\n      \\\"source_sha256\\\": \\\"737997cf5b7d4129f12ed5485ebbdd5e9d2ce3859a82ded6ac535d222327b713\\\",\\n      \\\"line_start\\\": 3,\\n      \\\"line_end\\\": 3,\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"> **Research prototype for reference only, not an official DeepSeek product.** This code grew out of our team's day-to-day development work, with much of the engineering done by coding agents. Treat it as research code, not production-ready software. It may still contain bugs, and its coding style and engineering practices may be inconsistent. Review and adapt it before using it in your own environment.\\\",\\n      \\\"verified\\\": \\\"Single line 3 of S1, including the leading blockquote marker exactly as in the source.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"C11\\\",\\n      \\\"source_id\\\": \\\"deepseek_readme\\\",\\n      \\\"source_sha256\\\": \\\"737997cf5b7d4129f12ed5485ebbdd5e9d2ce3859a82ded6ac535d222327b713\\\",\\n      \\\"line_start\\\": 5,\\n      \\\"line_end\\\": 5,\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"> We have adapted it for publication, so it is not identical to our internal version or the implementation described in *Exploring Super-agent Design: Towards a More Autonomous Agent System*. Some designs discussed in the article are directions for future development and are not implemented in this prototype.\\\",\\n      \\\"verified\\\": \\\"Single line 5 of S1. This is the entire in-scope evidence for the prototype-versus-article split; it names no specific feature.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"C12\\\",\\n      \\\"source_id\\\": \\\"deepseek_readme\\\",\\n      \\\"source_sha256\\\": \\\"737997cf5b7d4129f12ed5485ebbdd5e9d2ce3859a82ded6ac535d222327b713\\\",\\n      \\\"line_start\\\": 7,\\n      \\\"line_end\\\": 7,\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"dsh-superagent is a proactive coding agent for one GitHub repository, packaged as a bundle for [DeepSeek Harness](https://www.deepseek.com/en/harness/). It listens to GitHub and, optionally, Feishu. When someone allowed asks the agent for work, it opens a work item, works on it in its own agent session and directory, and answers in the original conversation, for example with a pull request. A web panel shows what needs a person.\\\",\\n      \\\"verified\\\": \\\"Single line 7 of S1; earlier revision truncated this sentence at 'pull request.' — now the full line through 'A web panel shows what needs a person.' is included.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"C13\\\",\\n      \\\"source_id\\\": \\\"deepseek_philosophy\\\",\\n      \\\"source_sha256\\\": \\\"0a12126843556fde2bcc2ca52dae2c297b9b5ca9170c3e33d624b2a4d85ca76b\\\",\\n      \\\"line_start\\\": 11,\\n      \\\"line_end\\\": 11,\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"- **It acts only when asked, or when a written rule allows it.** A request counts only when it addresses the agent directly and comes from a person the team allowed: one on an allowed list, or anyone in a conversation the team opened to requests. Work nobody asked for needs a rule the team wrote, and starts in a mode that only records what the agent would have done.\\\",\\n      \\\"verified\\\": \\\"Single line 11 of S2 with its leading list marker.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"C14\\\",\\n      \\\"source_id\\\": \\\"deepseek_philosophy\\\",\\n      \\\"source_sha256\\\": \\\"0a12126843556fde2bcc2ca52dae2c297b9b5ca9170c3e33d624b2a4d85ca76b\\\",\\n      \\\"line_start\\\": 12,\\n      \\\"line_end\\\": 12,\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"- **It speaks only when a person must act or can use a result.** It confirms a request once and names what it will do. It stays quiet while it works. It writes again when a result is ready, when it needs a decision, or when it cannot finish. Messages are short and go to the conversation where the request was made.\\\",\\n      \\\"verified\\\": \\\"Single line 12 of S2 with its leading list marker.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"C15\\\",\\n      \\\"source_id\\\": \\\"deepseek_philosophy\\\",\\n      \\\"source_sha256\\\": \\\"0a12126843556fde2bcc2ca52dae2c297b9b5ca9170c3e33d624b2a4d85ca76b\\\",\\n      \\\"line_start\\\": 15,\\n      \\\"line_end\\\": 15,\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"- **It reports honestly.** A draft is marked unfinished, a failure is reported as a failure, and a limit is never bypassed to avoid asking.\\\",\\n      \\\"verified\\\": \\\"Single line 15 of S2 with its leading list marker.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"C16\\\",\\n      \\\"source_id\\\": \\\"deepseek_philosophy\\\",\\n      \\\"source_sha256\\\": \\\"0a12126843556fde2bcc2ca52dae2c297b9b5ca9170c3e33d624b2a4d85ca76b\\\",\\n      \\\"line_start\\\": 19,\\n      \\\"line_end\\\": 20,\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"- **Few concepts.** The design has only its domain concepts, such as a Source, and their concrete implementations, such as GitHub and Feishu. A business need becomes an attribute of one of them, or a prompt the agent follows. The design does not add a concept for it.\\\\n- **Few settings.** A default replaces a setting when one value suits almost every team. Behaviour that a team describes in words is prompt text, not a setting.\\\",\\n      \\\"verified\\\": \\\"Two contiguous list items on lines 19-20 of S2; both list markers retained.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"C17\\\",\\n      \\\"source_id\\\": \\\"deepseek_philosophy\\\",\\n      \\\"source_sha256\\\": \\\"0a12126843556fde2bcc2ca52dae2c297b9b5ca9170c3e33d624b2a4d85ca76b\\\",\\n      \\\"line_start\\\": 28,\\n      \\\"line_end\\\": 28,\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"- **Start narrow.** Begin with a short allowed list and with proactive work only recorded. Widen both once what the agent would have done looks right.\\\",\\n      \\\"verified\\\": \\\"Single line 28 of S2 with its leading list marker; operator responsibility section.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"flow_map\\\": {\\n    \\\"source_to_trigger\\\": \\\"A Source emits a Trigger that must belong to at least one Thread; Intake normalizes the timestamp to canonical ISO and otherwise passes the payload through unchanged (C2).\\\",\\n    \\\"dedup_and_filter\\\": \\\"Deterministic, fixed-order gate: duplicate by trigger id returns before any scope evaluation, then SourceScope decides 'listened', and unlistened triggers are still persisted with an auditable disposition {filtered:{code}, fanout:[], at} (C2, C3, C1).\\\",\\n    \\\"thread_correlation\\\": \\\"Only for listened triggers: thread.lastAt is advanced and thread.correlated accumulates every sibling thread key of the trigger (C4).\\\",\\n    \\\"subscription_pass_through\\\": \\\"Fan-out iterates thread.subscriptions; a ticket is skipped when it is missing, or when it is not live and not resumable. Context-subscribed tickets are flagged context and never resume; only trigger.human resumes an ended ticket whose ended.by is not 'human' (C5).\\\",\\n    \\\"handoff\\\": \\\"Each reached ticket gets a trigger input keyed by (ticket, trigger) carrying human/context flags, and the disposition records the fanout set plus its context subset (C6).\\\",\\n    \\\"eval_fallback\\\": \\\"When no ticket owns the trigger (owners().length === 0) it is queued for Eval, so a listened-but-unowned event still receives a decision; afterwards each fanout ticket is woken (C7).\\\",\\n    \\\"audit_property\\\": \\\"One uniform per-trigger disposition record makes duplicate, filtered, stored, fanout and context outcomes replayable and auditable (C1, C3, C6).\\\",\\n    \\\"caveat\\\": \\\"Ordering claims describe source structure only; no runtime ordering or concurrency behaviour was observed.\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"prototype_vs_article\\\": {\\n    \\\"in_public_prototype\\\": \\\"Intake as a distinct EnginePart with stored/duplicate/filtered result type, SourceScope filtering with reason codes, thread correlation, subscription fan-out separating context reach from ownership, human-only resume, Eval fallback, persisted disposition and a trigger.received emission (C1-C9). README describes a proactive coding agent for one GitHub repository, optionally Feishu, working in its own session and directory and answering in the original conversation, with a web panel showing what needs a person (C12).\\\",\\n    \\\"article_side\\\": \\\"Documented split at the strength of README line 5 only: the publication version is not identical to the internal version or to the implementation described in 'Exploring Super-agent Design: Towards a More Autonomous Agent System', and some designs discussed in the article are future directions not implemented in this prototype (C11). README line 3 additionally warns the code is research code that may contain bugs (C10).\\\",\\n    \\\"boundary\\\": \\\"No specific article-only capability is named here. The article text and docs/007-architecture.md are not among the supplied materials, so at this node the split is asserted only as a general, documented divergence. Any named article feature, and any claim that such a feature is implemented, would exceed the supplied evidence and must be treated as a hypothesis awaiting those fixed revisions.\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"comparison_rows\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"topic\\\": \\\"Deterministic admission before any model work\\\",\\n      \\\"prototype\\\": \\\"Intake applies timestamp normalization, thread-presence validation, id duplicate check and SourceScope filter in fixed source order, all before fan-out; filtered triggers retain a disposition with a reason code (C1-C3).\\\",\\n      \\\"forge_implication\\\": \\\"FORGE should express listening policy as a code-level deterministic gate with a stable, persisted decision record per event, instead of leaving in-scope/in-out-of-scope judgement to model reasoning.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"deepseek_intake\\\"]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"topic\\\": \\\"Subscription pass-through: ownership versus context\\\",\\n      \\\"prototype\\\": \\\"Fans out to thread.subscriptions, tagging tickets reached only via context threads as context, and excluding tickets that are not live unless a human message resumes them (C4-C6).\\\",\\n      \\\"forge_implication\\\": \\\"FORGE needs an explicit distinction between an agent authorized to act (owner) and one merely informed (context); without it, passive subscribers are woken for events they cannot act on and consume attention.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"deepseek_intake\\\"]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"topic\\\": \\\"Fallback when no owner decides\\\",\\n      \\\"prototype\\\": \\\"If owners().length is zero the trigger is queued for Eval, and the disposition persists the fanout set, so listened events are not silently lost (C7, C9).\\\",\\n      \\\"forge_implication\\\": \\\"FORGE should define a named fallback path for events that pass the filter but reach no live owner; silent loss is both a correctness and an auditability defect.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"deepseek_intake\\\"]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"topic\\\": \\\"Attention budget as the design metric\\\",\\n      \\\"prototype\\\": \\\"The philosophy doc makes attention cost the test applied to every message, notification, question, setting and panel element, and requires speaking only when a person must act or can use a result (C14).\\\",\\n      \\\"forge_implication\\\": \\\"FORGE design review should count emitted messages and notifications as a first-class cost, and proactive work should require a written rule and start in record-only mode (C13).\\\",\\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"deepseek_philosophy\\\", \\\"deepseek_readme\\\"]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"topic\\\": \\\"Concept and setting minimality\\\",\\n      \\\"prototype\\\": \\\"Only domain concepts and their concrete implementations are permitted; a business need becomes an attribute or prompt text, and a default replaces a setting when one value suits almost every team (C16).\\\",\\n      \\\"forge_implication\\\": \\\"FORGE should prefer prompt-level policy and defaults over new configuration surfaces or abstractions, and review each new concept against an explicit budget.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"deepseek_philosophy\\\"]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"topic\\\": \\\"Honest reporting derived from records\\\",\\n      \\\"prototype\\\": \\\"Drafts are marked unfinished, failures reported as failures, and limits never bypassed (C15); trigger outcomes are persisted as disposition records rather than narrated (C3, C6).\\\",\\n      \\\"forge_implication\\\": \\\"FORGE status must be derived from persisted records, not from model narration, so a filtered, duplicated or failed event can never be presented as progress.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"deepseek_philosophy\\\", \\\"deepseek_intake\\\"]\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"risks\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"issue\\\": \\\"Treating a public research prototype as production semantics: README states it is not an official product, may contain bugs and is not identical to the internal or article version (C10, C11), while the philosophy doc states strong behavioural guarantees (C13-C15, C17).\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Carry every prototype claim as source inspection of fixed revision 8c32a9d, test critical paths independently, and label each guarantee as design intent rather than verified behaviour.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"issue\\\": \\\"Overstating the prototype/article comparison: the only supplied evidence of divergence is the README disclaimer (C11); the article and docs/007 are absent, so any named article-only feature would be unsupported.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Keep comparison claims at the level the disclaimer supports, mark any named article capability as a hypothesis, and never infer implementation status from the absence of code in a three-file sample.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"issue\\\": \\\"Fan-out amplification: every listened trigger reaches every subscribed ticket and wakes each one (C4-C7), so a heavily subscribed thread can multiply agent work and messages, contradicting the attention principle (C14).\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Cap per-thread fan-out, prefer context tagging for passive observers, and measure wake count per trigger as a budget input.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"issue\\\": \\\"Narrow resume semantics by construction: only a human trigger resumes an ended ticket, and human-stopped tickets are excluded (C5, C7), so a plausible-looking bot or CI event is not resumed.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Document the deliberate refusal of bot/CI resumption as policy and surface operator-visible reporting when such an event is routed to Eval instead of a ticket.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"recommendations\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Model FORGE ingestion as a deterministic pre-model gate (normalize, validate, dedupe, scope-filter) that persists a per-event decision record with reason codes.\\\",\\n      \\\"verification\\\": \\\"Table-driven check over the four outcomes: invalid (no threads), duplicate, filtered-with-reason, stored-with-fanout; each must yield a persisted disposition. Verify by source-level review of the gate ordering plus an independent unit test authored downstream.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Introduce an owner/context distinction in FORGE routing so only action-authorized agents are woken, and route unowned events to a named fallback queue.\\\",\\n      \\\"verification\\\": \\\"For a synthetic event reaching only context-subscribed or stopped agents, assert the context set is recorded correctly and the fallback queue receives exactly one entry.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Adopt attention cost as a review metric: enumerate messages and notifications per design change, and require a written rule for any proactive action, starting record-only.\\\",\\n      \\\"verification\\\": \\\"Reviewer checklist item per change lists each emitted message and its originating rule; confirm the record-only default for unrequested work (C17).\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Obtain docs/007-architecture.md and the architecture article as fixed revisions before making any named prototype-versus-article claim.\\\",\\n      \\\"verification\\\": \\\"Confirm the three supplied packets reference the article only in README lines 3 and 5 (C10, C11); request the missing fixed revisions and re-verify before asserting specifics.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"limitations\\\": [\\n    \\\"No execution, build, typecheck or test run was performed; every claim is static source inspection of three fixed git objects.\\\",\\n    \\\"Only src/core/intake.ts was supplied as implementation; scope.ts, tickets.ts, model.ts, part.ts and ids.ts are referenced but absent, so SourceScope reason codes and addInput/wake semantics are known only through call sites.\\\",\\n    \\\"The architecture article and docs/007-architecture.md are not in the supplied set, so the prototype/article split rests solely on README lines 3 and 5.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"receipts\\\": {\\n    \\\"inputs_read\\\": [\\n      \\\"inputs/projects/project_beta/l2/deepseek_intake.json (packet file_sha256 d794df820efd11166ef801d30e287a923c16c35dc9e666484be4fad6fdc9bf97)\\\",\\n      \\\"inputs/projects/project_beta/l2/scenario.json (sha256 cca2f2f4bb51bd46db7390dc62250f3e87108ac5f81808211a4811e3c80200a7)\\\",\\n      \\\"inputs/projects/project_beta/l2/deepseek_readme.json (packet file_sha256 3ef5dced147170146cc2b91aca3870cf8bfb84f952a8c16262a7175ab018cfbf)\\\",\\n      \\\"inputs/projects/project_beta/l2/deepseek_philosophy.json (packet file_sha256 2257025548c4799bbda7753936730a80b9f029406c2da08289acb658a40a3c1b)\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"inputs_modified\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n    \\\"prior_artifact_revised\\\": \\\"work/quest_4423cc2f7620/source_analysis.json receipt_365